ose. || PSIONICS (Dog Boy printed 33, #4 and #5): master psionic, I.S.P. M.E. plus 1D6x10 and +10 per additional level; Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Sixth Sense and Empathy (receiver only) plus one Sensitive power of choice. || NATURAL ABILITIES: fundamentally the Dog Boy''s, restated from printed 33-35, with the Kill Hound''s exceptions: scent abilities halved (the Dog Boy figures are stored with the halving stated; the book does not say whether the psychic-scent abilities #1-#3 are also halved, and they are stored unhalved - judgement, the line speaks of olfactory senses), bite 3D6+6, punch and kick 2D6 plus P.S. bonuses, leap, supernatural endurance (replaces the Dog Boy''s 20x/40x carry and two-hour stamina). The leap prints 15 feet as 3.6 m; stored as printed. Recognize Psychic Scent prints ''10% 44%'' in the text layer and on the page; read as 10% +4%. || SKILLS: American and Spanish at 85%: Language: Native Tongue 85 and Language: Spanish 85, per_level 0. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Track Humanoids is Tracking (people) 25+15 = 40. Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals 20+10 = 30. Escape Artist 30+5 = 35. Pilot Motorcycle/Hovercycle (+5%) is one printed line; stored as a choice of one of the two catalog skills at +5 (judgement). Climbing 40, no bonus printed. Running, Boxing. Land Navigation 36+10 = 46. Wilderness Survival 30+20 = 50. W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Energy Rifle, W.P. Knife or Sword as a choice of one, two W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Assassin, pick one, as a choice; the Kill Hound entry prints no price for any other style, so no hand_to_hand block. || RELATED: four, plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. Domestic -5% and Science (Basic Math only) -10% stored as negative bonuses; Espionage +5, Military +10, Wilderness +10, Rogue +5 with Hacking excluded - Streetwise is +10% in the book and receives only the category''s +5 here, the difference stated in the note. Pilot ''any simple ground vehicle and jet pack'' stored as Automobile, Bicycling, Motorcycles & Snowmobiles, Truck, Hover Craft (ground), Hovercycles and Jet Packs (judgement; tanks, tracked and construction vehicles, robots, boats and aircraft left out). Electrical, Mechanical, Medical, Pilot Related: none. Secondary: four, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, same list without bonuses or penalties. The never-taught-to-read note is a restriction line; literacy skills are not excluded from Technical. || EQUIPMENT: basically the Dog Boy''s (printed 36). Armor: Kill Hounds usually get heavy DPM armor or full environmental armor, stored as a choice of the Dog Pack riot armor or the D1 heavy or D2 light environmental suits. 100 ft of lightweight rope as five 20 ft lengths. A pair of vibro-knives or vibro-claws as a choice at qty 2. C-14 Fire Breather or CP-40 with telescopic sight and nightvision scope. Of the three implants every Kill Hound has, the clock calendar and gyro-compass are equipment rows and the toxic filter, which no catalog row describes, is named in the Cybernetics ability; the pick-one implant list is in the Cybernetics ability text. Equipment Available Upon Assignment (grenades, flares, explosives, heavy weapons, optics, cameras, light vehicle, rations, non-regulation gear) is not starting equipment and is not stored. || MONEY: same as the Dog Boy: a monthly salary of 200-300 credits (700 for officers) and player characters start with two months pay, so 400-600 credits; stored as 600, the figure the dog-boy class in production carries for the same sentence. || Identification coding (bar-code tattoo and I.C. chip with a one mile tracking range), typical missions and the pack pecking order are lore."
---

## Lore

Kill Hounds are the Lone Star labs'' answer to a blunt question: what if a Dog
Boy were built only to fight? Introduced in 104 P.A. with the coming siege of
Tolkeen in mind, they are bred from the largest and hardest breeds - mastiffs,
Rottweilers, wolfhounds, wolves - into towering, barrel-chested soldiers who
keep the predatory edge that the Coalition trains out of its other canines.

Where an ordinary Dog Boy is courteous and eager to please, a Kill Hound is
cocky, pushy and happiest when turned loose on a hunt. They work as shock
troops, wilderness hunter-killers, raiders and occasionally guards, and they
proved themselves against Juicers during the Juicer Uprising. In a pack they
sort themselves into a pecking order under an alpha, and the bigger the pack
the bolder and crueler it gets.

They still honor their human officers, though with stares, growls and slow
feet when an order bores them. Their noses are duller than a Dog Boy''s, so
they track by eye and by craft as much as by scent, and they keep the psychic
senses that make every mutant canine a hunter of magic and the supernatural.

## GM Notes

A Kill Hound is a strong combatant with real costs: it ignores wounds until it
drops, forgets the dull parts of a mission, rises to any challenge, and can
lose itself in bloodlust or a berserker rage. Roll percentile at creation for
Rage Syndrome (01-20) and for Jekyll and Hyde Syndrome (01-33).

Typical assignments are seek and destroy, commando raids and rescues, tracking,
assassination and sabotage, anti-magic and anti-supernatural sweeps, and purges
of D-Bee settlements; escort, guard and infantry duty are occasional. They are
kept off city police duty apart from the odd violent sweep of the Burbs.

Streetwise taken as a related skill is +10% in the book; the Rogue category
gives +5%, so add the other 5% by hand.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kill-hound');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kill-hound';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-kill-hound-class.sql');
